1x9x|n|To perceive by the olfactory nerves, or organs of smell; to have a sensation of, excited through the nasal organs when affected by the appropriate materials or qualities; to obtain the scent of; as, to smell a rose; to smell perfumes. ; To detect or perceive, as if by the sense of smell; to scent out; -- often with out. ; To give heed to.	a:1d30,91,3;21ve,89,2~1d30,91,3;21ve,89,2	n:1kq1,46,4~1kq1,46,4	N:23dg,25,1~23dg,25,1
